{"ts":"2026-11-03T20:02:25.535Z","event":"hook","session":"e404-a1854f6cb290","seq":1,"tag":"fam","harness":"agy","decision":"allow","tool":"call_mcp_tool","server":"council_council","tool_call":{"args":{"Arguments":{"action":"move","round":"r2","text":"Recommend that plans like the vsect maturation plan be checked by one independent reviewer from another model family as the standard baseline, reserving full councils for high-stakes irremediable shifts or when the cross-family reviewer identifies structural deadlocks. A reviewer from a distinct model family provides the critical cognitive diversity needed to catch blind spots, unstated assumptions, and shared training-distribution biases that same-family reviewers routinely gloss over, achieving the majority of defect-reduction benefits without council overhead."},"ServerName":"council_council","ToolName":"council_submit"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"conversation":"832da779-3a97-43c0-9b28-c38ed0a676e2","step":10,"model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low"}
{"ts":"2026-11-03T20:02:28.213Z","event":"hook","session":"e408-a185ef123068","seq":1,"tag":"fam","harness":"agy","decision":"allow","tool":"call_mcp_tool","server":"council_council","tool_call":{"args":{"Arguments":{},"ServerName":"council_council","ToolName":"council_wait"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"conversation":"832da779-3a97-43c0-9b28-c38ed0a676e2","step":12,"model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low"}
{"ts":"2026-11-03T20:02:44.690Z","event":"hook","session":"e455-a189c522d1c8","seq":1,"tag":"fam","harness":"agy","decision":"allow","tool":"call_mcp_tool","server":"council_council","tool_call":{"args":{"Arguments":{"action":"speak","round":"r3","text":"There is striking alignment across all four vantages: every member moved that one independent reviewer from another model family should be the baseline check, with councils reserved for escalation (unresolved deadlocks or high-stakes irreversible work). Key enrichments from indep and plan should be incorporated: charging the reviewer with specific actionable checks (dependencies, unstated assumptions, verification test validity) rather than subjective grading, and unanchored review where the reviewer writes findings before seeing author rationales. I welcome an amendment synthesizing these operational details into the pending motion."},"ServerName":"council_council","ToolName":"council_submit"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"conversation":"832da779-3a97-43c0-9b28-c38ed0a676e2","step":14,"model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low"}
